## Top 5 This Week

1. **Purview DLM Billing Model Change**{{< cat "Security & Compliance" >}} - If your retention policies cover non-Microsoft 365 generative AI prompts and responses, your costs are about to be calculated differently. The new model bills on data volume retained (per GB/month) rather than per-message counts. Review your DLM policy scope and estimate retained data volume now before the new meter hits.

2. **RDP Multipath with Redundant TCP Goes GA**{{< cat "Security & Compliance" >}} - Windows 365 and Azure Virtual Desktop environments in TCP-restricted or VPN-heavy networks now have a production-ready resilience layer. This directly addresses session drops caused by packet loss and UDP restrictions without requiring firewall changes.

3. **People Skills Admin Deletion Control**{{< cat "Security & Compliance" >}} - Admins now have a tenant-wide nuclear option for People Skills data: full deletion of the skills library, confirmed/inferred/imported skills, and removal from profile cards and Copilot experiences. Useful if you're offboarding from Skills or responding to a data governance requirement.

4. **SharePoint Library Default Label Auto-Apply (Preview Sept, GA Oct)** - Auto-labeling of existing files at rest to match the library's default sensitivity label closes a long-standing gap. Plan your library label configurations now so you're ready to validate behavior in the September preview.

5. **Microsoft + AXA XL Incident Response Integration**{{< cat "Security & Compliance" >}} - Microsoft Incident Response services are now available directly through AXA XL cyber insurance policies. If your organization holds AXA XL coverage, validate whether this integration is active and how it fits your existing IR runbooks.

---

## Security & Compliance

- **[Real World Incident Response: Microsoft and AXA XL Strengthen Cyber Resilience](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/22/real-world-incident-response-microsoft-and-axa-xl-strengthen-cyber-resilience/)** [GA] - If your organization carries AXA XL cyber insurance, Microsoft Incident Response services are now integrated directly into policyholder response workflows. The collaboration is designed to align technical containment, business continuity, and insurance claims processes under a single coordinated response. Check your insurance policy terms and update your IR runbook to reference this channel alongside your existing escalation paths.

- **[RDP Multipath with Redundant TCP Is Now Generally Available for Windows 365 and Azure Virtual Desktop](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/rdp-multipath-with-redundant-tcp-is-now-generally-available-for/ba-p/4534610)** [GA] - Environments where UDP is blocked or VPN routing degrades RDP sessions now have a supported, production-ready fix. RDP Multipath with redundant TCP extends session resiliency by aggregating multiple TCP paths, reducing the impact of packet loss, ISP instability, and proxy interference. No firewall changes are required; validate that your Windows 365 and AVD environments are on a supported client and host version to pick this up.

- **[Microsoft Purview: Data Lifecycle Management - DLM Meter Change](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560324)** [GA] - The DLM billing model is shifting from per-message pricing to volume-based pricing at $0.25 per GB per month for retained non-Microsoft 365 generative AI prompts and responses. If your retention policies sweep AI interactions at scale, run a data volume estimate against your current retained content before this meter activates. Organizations retaining large volumes of short AI messages may see cost changes in either direction depending on their payload sizes.

- **[Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft 365): People Skills - Removal and Deletion Admin Control](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=565905)** [GA] - Admins can now permanently delete the entire People Skills dataset for a tenant, including the skills library and all confirmed, inferred, and imported skills. Once triggered, skills disappear from profile cards and all skills-based Copilot and Viva experiences with no automatic reversal. This is the control you need for compliance-driven offboarding from People Skills; treat it as irreversible and scope the decision accordingly before initiating.

- **[Microsoft Purview: Information Protection - Apply Default SharePoint Library Labels to Data at Rest](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=559105)** [Preview] - Auto-labeling of existing files to match the configured default sensitivity label on their document library hits preview in September 2026 and goes GA in October 2026. This closes the gap where files uploaded before a library label was configured remained unlabeled. Audit your SharePoint library default label configurations now so you can assess scope and avoid unintended bulk label application when preview lands.

---

## Action Required

- **[Purview DLM Meter Change](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560324)** [GA, act now] - Before this billing change takes effect, pull a retained-data volume estimate for any DLM policies covering non-Microsoft 365 AI prompts and responses. The shift from per-message to per-GB pricing could materially change your Purview spend depending on average payload size. Engage your licensing or FinOps contact if you need pre-change cost modeling.

- **[People Skills Admin Deletion Control](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=565905)** [GA, governance decision required] - Now that tenant-wide People Skills deletion is available, document your organization's position on Skills data retention before anyone exercises this control. Deletion is permanent and removes skills from Copilot and Viva experiences immediately. Define who has authorization to trigger this and capture it in your admin runbook.

- **[SharePoint Library Default Label Auto-Apply](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=559105)** [Preview September 2026] - With preview arriving in roughly 60 days, start auditing SharePoint library default sensitivity labels now. Libraries with misconfigured or missing default labels will have that state applied retroactively to existing content at rest when this feature activates. Identify any libraries where bulk label application would be unexpected and correct library configurations before preview rollout begins.